  seconds: 9341
  topic: 'Vote: Final Percentage of Tax Impact'
  desc: The board discussed and voted on the final percentage of tax impact for the
    budget, considering city council guidance. Initially proposing 7%, the motion
    was amended to 6% based on feedback from the city council.
  children:
  - seconds: 9370
    speaker: Tyler Smith
    text: Board member Tyler Smith proposed a 7% tax impact to add to contingency
      accounts, emphasizing the importance of taking every opportunity to build financial
      reserves. Daniel Feller seconded the motion, agreeing on the need for contingency
      to prevent future financial pain.
  - seconds: 9480
    speaker: Angela Atkinson Duina
    text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina suggested the board consider the city
      council's unusual action of supporting the district with $2 million and their
      signals to stay at 6%. She noted the rarity of such a complete remediation of
      a deficit.
  - seconds: 9580
    speaker: Claire Holman
    text: Board member Claire Holman concurred with the Superintendent, having attended
      the city council meeting. She noted council members' concerns about tax increases
      and the higher voter turnout expected due to a primary election, suggesting
      a lower percentage would be prudent.
  - seconds: 9639
    speaker: Eleni Richardson
    text: Board member Eleni Richardson stated that four city council members indicated
      they would vote against a budget above 6%. Tyler Smith then rescinded his 7%
      motion and accepted a friendly amendment to make it 6%.
  - seconds: 9753
    speaker: George Risch
    text: Board member George Risch supported the 6% tax impact, acknowledging the
      city's grant and stating that adhering to 6% honors previous budget commitments.
      He found changing it now would be complicated.
  - seconds: 9796
    speaker: Daniel Feller
    text: Board member Daniel Feller acknowledged the city council's understanding
      of public sentiment regarding taxes, suggesting their 6% guidance reflected
      public concerns about high taxes.
  - seconds: 9970
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: Chair DeAngelis expressed gratitude for the city's support and her reluctance
      to risk budget approval by exceeding 6%, despite her personal desire for more
      contingency. She mentioned concerns about cutting a percussion ed tech position
      and the band program.
  - seconds: 10070
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: The motion to approve a 6% tax impact, as amended, passed unanimously.
