      Portland school district. He committed to working with administration to maintain
      positions and stability.
  - seconds: 10255
    speaker: Eleni Richardson
    text: Board member Eleni Richardson expressed regret that more positions couldn't
      be saved and concern for the schools next year, but trusted the leadership.
      She asked for a 'vibe check' to ensure reductions aren't causing harm, acknowledging
      the district was previously heavily staffed.
  - seconds: 10370
    speaker: Daniel Feller
    text: Board member Daniel Feller stated he trusts the administration on special
      education staffing but urged high alert for staffing issues and reactivity to
      safety concerns, especially with new CDS regulations.
  - seconds: 10403
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: Chair DeAngelis attempted to amend the motion to change the DEI strategist
      position to a coordinator, aiming for revenue neutrality, but it failed for
      lack of a second.
  - seconds: 10456
    speaker: Rosemarie DeAngelis
    text: The motion to adopt personnel reductions, as presented and consistent with
      the final budget, passed unanimously.
